# PROXY-ROUTER BINARY DOWNLOADS
#
# Required, not optional: the app's readiness gate depends only on
# proxy-router (see orchestrator.ts calculateOrchestratorStatus), and
# downloadProxyRouter() has no try/catch around it — it's the one download
# the setup wizard cannot route around. Without one of these set for the
# platform actually running, orchestrator.ts's downloadProxyRouter() silently
# no-ops (its whole body is wrapped in `if (this.cfg.proxyRouter.downloadUrl)`)
# and marks itself 'success' anyway, so startProxyRouter() then throws ENOENT
# trying to write proxy-router/.env into a services/proxy-router/ directory
# that was never created — with no error surfaced to the user. Confirmed as
# the exact cause of a real tester's setup freeze on a first-time install
# (2026-08-19): these were never set here at all, on any platform, and it was
# masked in every developer's own testing because a dev machine that has
# already run the app once has a cached binary and never needs the URL.
#
# mac-arm64 / mac-x64 point at cowboycoderhq's own release (proxy-router has
# fork-specific changes not on any upstream binary) — rebuilt from
# stake-duration HEAD 2026-08-19 (commit 5129e01c) matching build.sh's own
# invocation (`go build -trimpath -tags docker`, same ldflags) and uploaded to
# desktop-v7.5.0-cc.1, replacing stale 2026-07-18 assets that predated recent
# proxy-router changes. Runtime-verified (loads config, queries the
# blockchain for configured models, clean SIGTERM) before uploading, both
# architectures. -trimpath added on top of build.sh's own flags: a plain
# `go build` embeds the building machine's full local username/home path in
# every dependency's source-file references (confirmed via `strings` on the
# first build attempt here) — -trimpath removes nearly all of it. A handful
# of paths from gnark-crypto's hand-written elliptic-curve assembly survive
# even with -trimpath (a known Go tooling gap for .s files) — low severity
# (a username in a third-party dependency's source path, nothing else), not
# eliminated further here.
SERVICE_PROXY_DOWNLOAD_URL_MAC_ARM64=https://github.com/cowboycoderhq/Morpheus-Lumerin-Node/releases/download/desktop-v7.5.0-cc.1/mac-arm64-morpheus-router
SERVICE_PROXY_DOWNLOAD_URL_MAC_X64=https://github.com/cowboycoderhq/Morpheus-Lumerin-Node/releases/download/desktop-v7.5.0-cc.1/mac-x64-morpheus-router
# Linux and Windows have NO proxy-router binary uploaded anywhere on this
# fork yet — a first-time install on either platform hits the exact freeze
# described above, with nothing to point these at as a stopgap. Needs a real
# build uploaded (matching the mac ones above) before setting these:
# SERVICE_PROXY_DOWNLOAD_URL_LINUX_X64=
# SERVICE_PROXY_DOWNLOAD_URL_LINUX_ARM64=
# SERVICE_PROXY_DOWNLOAD_URL_WINDOWS_X64=
# SERVICE_PROXY_DOWNLOAD_URL_WINDOWS_ARM64=

# COMMON
BYPASS_AUTH=false
DEBUG=false
DEFAULT_SELLER_CURRENCY=BTC #remove it
IGNORE_DEBUG_LOGS=false #remove it
# SENTRY_DSN is OPTIONAL, but the schema types it as a URI — so an empty value
# fails validation where an absent key passes. Leave it commented out unless you
# have a real DSN.
# SENTRY_DSN=https://examplePublicKey@o0.ingest.sentry.io/0
TRACKING_ID=
# FAILOVER_ENABLED is a BOOLEAN with a default of true. An empty value is not a
# boolean and fails validation; omit the key to take the default, or set
# true/false explicitly.
# FAILOVER_ENABLED=false
